{"packet_id":"D006-01","doc_id":"D006","jurisdiction":"Berkeley, CA","category":"rent_increase_limits","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Measure BB Annual General Adjustment cap","requirement":"The annual rent increase for a fully covered unit is the Annual General Adjustment set by the Rent Board, capped at 5%; banked AGAs may still raise rent above 5% to the ceiling, and petitions are allowed only for completed capital improvements.","key_value":"5% maximum AGA","coverage_conditions":"Fully covered units, including most units in multifamily properties built before 1980; units with a certificate of occupancy issued after 1980 and most single-family homes and condominiums are only partially covered and have no rent ceiling.","applicability":{"conditions":[{"type":"built","role":"covered","op":"before","date":"1980","basis":"construction"},{"type":"built","role":"exempt","op":"after","date":"1980","basis":"certificate_of_occupancy"},{"type":"owner","role":"exempt","who":"owner living on the same property who shares kitchen or bath with tenant","unit_limit":null}],"per_tenancy":null,"coverage_quotes":["Most units in multifamily properties built before 1980","New Construction Units (units with a certificate of occupancy issued after 1980)","Where the tenant shares a kitchen or bath facilities with the landlord, the unit will be exempt from the Rent Ordinance only if the landlord lived in a unit on the same property at the start of the tenancy."]},"exemptions":"Partially covered units have no rent ceiling: New Construction Units certified after 1980, most single-family homes, most condominiums, and units whose subsidies federal or state law exempts from rent control.","penalty":null,"effective_date":null,"valid_through":null,"citation":"Berkeley Mun. Code ch. 13.76","quoted_span":"The maximum AGA is 5%. This means that, if the formula in the Rent Ordinance results in an AGA that is greater than 5%, the AGA approved by the Board for that year can be no more than 5%.","interaction":"Units whose subsidies are exempt from rent control under federal or state law are only partially covered.","relations":[],"confidence":0.8,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D006-01","doc_id":"D006","jurisdiction":"Berkeley, CA","category":"just_cause_eviction","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Measure BB just cause eviction changes","requirement":"Tenants in covered units may be evicted only for just cause; nonpayment eviction requires debt of at least one month's Fair Market Rent. Landlords may not evict for refusal to sign a similar lease and must file eviction notices within three business days.","key_value":"Rental debt of at least 1 month's Fair Market Rent","coverage_conditions":"Tenants in rental units that are fully or partially covered by the Berkeley Rent Ordinance.","applicability":{"conditions":[{"type":"other","text":"Units fully or partially covered by the Rent Ordinance"},{"type":"owner","role":"exempt","who":"owner living on the same property who shares kitchen or bath with tenant","unit_limit":null}],"per_tenancy":null,"coverage_quotes":["In Berkeley, tenants in units that are fully or partially covered by the Rent Ordinance cannot be evicted unless there is \"just cause” (previously called “good cause”).","Where the tenant shares a kitchen or bath facilities with the landlord, the unit will be exempt from the Rent Ordinance only if the landlord lived in a unit on the same property at the start of the tenancy."]},"exemptions":"Units exempt from the Rent Ordinance, including units where the tenant shares kitchen or bath facilities with a landlord who lived on the property at the start of the tenancy.","penalty":null,"effective_date":null,"valid_through":null,"citation":"Berkeley Mun. Code ch. 13.76","quoted_span":"For a landlord to evict a tenant for nonpayment of rent, the tenant must owe an amount of rental debt equal to or greater than one month of the Fair Market Rent (FMR) value for a unit of equivalent size in the metro area Oakland-Fremont, CA HUD Metro FMR as determined by the US Department of Housing and Urban Development for the fiscal year in which the rent is demanded.","interaction":null,"relations":[],"confidence":0.8,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
